      "source": "Wu Blockchain (Telegram)",
      "type": "telegram",
      "headline": "Highlight Clip: Michael Saylor: Bitcoin Can Resist AI Attacks, Satoshi Was Right to Limit Features Michael Saylor: Bitcoin Can Resist AI Attacks, Satoshi Was Right to Limit Features On November 5, 2026, Strategy founder Michael Saylor joined Oranje Summit 2026 remotely. The event was held in São Paulo, Brazil. Saylor said frontier AI models make hackers more capable and that complex software used to move funds, including exchange and wallet software, is especially vulnerable. He argued that Bitcoin's design makes it resilient to AI threats and that Satoshi Nakamoto was right to limit its base-layer features because complex software expands the attack surface. He added that Bitcoin's computing power and security helped it win the race to become the global standard for digital capital. — link",
